Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the next lower grade level GS-12 or pay band in the federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate performing duties such as: 1) Representing the organization as a Hazardous Materials data expert at meetings, conferences or workshops involving supply hazardous material policies, requirements and procedures;
2) Establishing and maintaining contact with officials and managers to explain requirements, interpret policy, justify recommendations and negotiate for funding or other requests;
3) Working with representatives to develop cooperative agreements, standardized procedures, and other efforts;
4) Providing justification, requirements, and providing assistance on the creation, review, and justification of budgets for assigned programs;
5) Providing direction, advice and guidance to personnel on any aspect of afloat data and supply pollution prevention. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.
